iOS native views: keyboard input to a native view (needs 0063).

What:
- Keyboard: `set_focused_native_view` gives keyboard input to a native view (`KeyboardInput::NativeView(id)`):
  GPUI's text input view resigns and never becomes first responder, so the app can make its own UIView (a
  UITextField, a WKWebView) first responder. When GPUI focus comes back, a focused GPUI field takes first responder
  again, even though UIKit cleared its keyboard wish when the app's view took first responder from it. Dropping the
  focused view's last handle also gives the keyboard back, whatever GPUI tells the window, so a GPUI field focused
  next always gets it.

Where: one-line hooks in upstream's window.rs and text_input.rs, 0062's native_views.rs (the drop), and
ios/native_view_state.rs, which now holds the two lifecycles, `KeyboardInput` and `Rotation`, as pure transitions,
table-tested on the host by scripts/patch-test.sh (`ios-pure`).

Tests: `KeyboardInput::next`'s table, one row per (state, event), rejected and dropped-view events among them.
Checked (0062–0064 together) on the iOS simulator as 0062 says: after the native UITextField took the keyboard and
every native view was dropped, typing goes to GPUI's field.

Upstream PR: not filed (filing paused, patch rule 14).

